---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro"
import { SITE } from "../site"

const mail = `mailto:${SITE.email}`
---

<Base title="Privacy">
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      Responsible in accordance with the data protection laws:
      <br />
      Martin Lechner
      <br />
      Klosterstrasse 6d
      <br />
      82284 Grafrath, Germany
    </p>

    <h2>General information</h2>
    <p>
      As the operator of lechner.work it is important to me that you know exactly which personal
      data is collected on this website, how it is processed, and how you can influence it. In
      particular, I would like to stress that I have no interest in your data. These will only be
      collected and stored for technical reasons. In doing so, I adhere to the principle of data
      minimization.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting and access log</h2>
    <p>
      lechner.work is currently delivered by Netlify. The terms of
      <a href="https://www.netlify.com/gdpr-ccpa/">Netlify's stance on GDPR</a>
      apply. I have no access to any data (e.g. access logs) the hoster might collect.
    </p>

    <h2>Encryption</h2>
    <p>All data transferred between the web server and your browser is encrypted using TLS.</p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>This website does not set any cookies and does not store anything else on your device.</p>

    <h2>Statistics</h2>
    <p>
      To see how many people visit each page, this website uses
      <a href="https://www.goatcounter.com">GoatCounter</a>, an open source and privacy-friendly web
      analytics service. When a page loads, a small script from gc.zgo.at reports the address of the
      page and the page you came from (referrer) to GoatCounter. Only these two are stored, as daily
      and hourly totals; individual page views are not recorded.
    </p>
    <p>
      Like every request, this one also contains your IP address and your browser's user agent.
      GoatCounter uses them only to recognise repeated visits from the same visitor, so that
      reloading a page isn't counted twice. For this it keeps a random ID for your IP address and
      user agent in memory for up to eight hours. Neither your IP address nor your user agent is
      ever stored. GoatCounter doesn't set cookies, doesn't store anything in your browser and
      doesn't share the data with third parties. It runs on servers of Hetzner Online GmbH in
      Germany and Finland. I only see aggregated numbers, such as views per page and referring
      websites.
    </p>
    <p>
      The legal basis is my legitimate interest in knowing which content is read (Art. 6(1)(f)
      GDPR). If you don't want to be counted, block gc.zgo.at in your browser or content blocker.
      Details are in{" "}
      <a href="https://www.goatcounter.com/help/privacy">GoatCounter's privacy policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>External links</h2>
    <p>
      Blog posts link to content on other websites, for example videos. Once you follow such a link,
      the privacy policy of that website applies.
    </p>

    <h2>Information, correction and deletion</h2>
    <p>
      You have the right to receive information about your personal data stored by me at any time.
      You also have the right to have your personal data or parts thereof corrected or deleted. To
      do so, send an email to
      <a href={mail}>{SITE.email}</a>. Please note that when you send this email, personal data will
      be stored in my mail account (see next section).
    </p>

    <h2>Email</h2>
    <p>
      If you contact me by email at <a href={mail}>{SITE.email}</a>, I will store all the
      information you send me. I do this in order to be able to react appropriately to your
      contacting me. I keep direct emails to me permanently in my email account, which is hosted by
      Proton in Switzerland.
    </p>

    <h2>Modification of the data protection declaration</h2>
    <p>
      I reserve the right to update this privacy policy to comply with current legal requirements or
      to explain changes to my infrastructure. Your renewed visit will then be subject to the new
      privacy policy.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions about data protection</h2>
    <p>
      If you have any questions about data protection, please send an email to
      <a href={mail}>{SITE.email}</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
